		{
			dependencies: ["1E7344C133C99565"]
			description: [
				"Simply put, the hatch pulls items from the ME Network into its own internal storage, and then lets the machine use the items in its internal storage (in other words, it is an ME Interface)"
				""
				"The &6pull limit&r of the ME Input Bus/Hatch has been increased to &b9.2E/P"
				""
				"Left-click with a &dData Stick&r to save the hatch's configuration, right-click to apply the configuration"
				""
				"Right-click an ME hatch with &dWire Cutters&r to toggle the ME hatch between connecting to the network from the front and connecting from any side"
				""
				"You can adjust the &6pull interval&r at the bottom left of the hatch GUI; by default it shows 0tick, which means the pull interval is not changed, with &ba minimum of 1tick&r (this affects the speed of pulling from the ME Network)"
				""
				"All three types of ME Output Hatch have long-level capacity and unlimited slots (they output once per second, and the maximum amount of machine output accepted in a single transfer is &bint&r)"
				""
				"The ME Dual Output Hatch has been optimised for better performance, and can &6manually&r eject items/fluids stuck inside it into the ME network"
				""
				"The ME Chamber Manager Terminal, as the name suggests, manages every ME hatch in the network except Pattern Buffers"
			]
